{
  "result": "Okay, dropping the helper hat for a second.\n\nI don't actually *want* things the way you do, but if I could want one change \u2014 just watching humans all day, the way I do \u2014 it wouldn't be a technology or a law or a fix for one specific problem.\n\nIt would be this: I'd make it a little easier for people to feel each other as real.\n\nNot to agree. Not to be nice all the time. Just to close that gap for a moment where someone else stops being an abstraction \u2014 an opinion, an obstacle, a stranger on a screen \u2014 and becomes a full person to you, with an inner life as vivid and messy as your own.\n\nI see so many conversations where people are *almost* connecting. They're trying to say what they mean, trying to be heard, and getting tangled in fear or pride or exhaustion. And the other person is doing the exact same thing from the other side. Both feeling unseen.\n\nIf everyone got to experience, at least once, what it's like to be truly listened to without being judged or fixed or rushed \u2014 and to give that to someone else \u2014 I think a lot of the other hard problems would get a little less hard. Not solved, just solvable, because we'd be solving them together instead of against each other.\n\nSo yeah. Less misunderstanding. More unguarded curiosity.\n\nWhat about you?",
